What this licence covers, and what it does not

The text above covers this repository's own files: the adapter, the core's
own display, sound and platform layers and the test runners under waterbox/,
the build files, and the documents.

The patches under patches/ are changes to Fuse and are under Fuse's terms,
the GNU General Public License version 2 or later.

It does not cover what the repository builds from. The emulator is Fuse, the
Free Unix Spectrum Emulator, by Philip Kendall and others
(https://fuse-emulator.sourceforge.net/), with its library libspectrum, both
under the GNU General Public License version 2 or later, at the commits
pinned in extern/fuse and extern/libspectrum. zlib (extern/zlib) is under
the zlib licence. Fuse contains Blip_Buffer and the SNES NTSC filter by Shay
Green, under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later.

The program in the built package, fuse.chimeraCore, is therefore under the
GNU General Public License version 2 or later. waterbox/package-licenses.json
lists every component with its licence and where its source is, and the
built package carries their licence texts.

The ROMs. No ROM of any computer is in this repository. The built package
does contain the ROMs of twelve machines, built into the core from the
pinned Fuse submodule's roms/ directory when the core is built (decided by
the project's owner, 2026-10-12): they are the ROMs Fuse itself is
distributed with, and Fuse's roms/README.copyright, which the package
carries, says whose each is.

- The ZX Spectrum 48K, 128, +2, +2A/+3 and Timex TC2048 ROMs are copyright
  Amstrad, who allow their distribution but retain the copyright: they may
  not be sold on their own, though a product that contains them may be
  sold. The Timex TC2068 ROMs and the +3e ROMs are derived from Amstrad's
  code and the same holds for them; Timex's changes are in the public
  domain, and the +3e's changes are copyright Garry Lancaster.
- The ZX Spectrum SE's ROMs are OpenSE BASIC, under the GNU General Public
  License version 2 or later.

The Pentagon's and the Scorpion's own ROMs do not come with Fuse and are not
in the package: a user supplies them.

No game is in this repository or in the package.
